WEBVTT

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.240
Our only fighters are you and Yuri!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.530
Hey! Look at this, Quon.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.870
Is that a music box?

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.870
Could I listen to it?

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.010
I demand perfection and completeness in every respect.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.870
Please remember that, Rookie-kun.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.460
My voice...

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.260
Both.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.190
I want to save them all.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.970
And that won't change in a thousand years.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.940
What are you people?

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.350
We're Attractors.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.440
According to Kannazuki, we've awakened.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.030
I want to save everyone, no matter what.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.320
Others like you and Yuuma-kun who don't know what to do...

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.670
Everyone.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.860
Quon-sama?

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.260
I heard your heart moaning in pain.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:40.480
Be careful.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.790
You're defenseless in your sleep.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.510
You're attracted to a strong will.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.010
I understand.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.220
But I can't do anything about it.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.110
Don't worry.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.540
I'll stay by your side until you sleep.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:01.730
No, please don't worry about me.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.010
Please.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.680
Crime scene to HQ.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.200
We've confirmed the death of a gun victim at 2550.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.990
We'll bring the victim in the car and turn him in for autopsy.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.700
This is HQ. Roger.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.850
Did that sting?

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:40.660
A bit.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:44.640
If it's really bad, do you want me to disconnect your nerves?

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.180
Please don't.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.000
You'd be sending me into a world of darkness, where I couldn't move my limbs.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.320
I was just being nice.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.810
By the way, what are you reading?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.860
<i>In Search of Lost Time.</i>

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.910
Ah, Proust.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.240
I read that when I was young.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.240
It's one long-ass novel.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.810
You know, I don't get you.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.330
You could just download it into your brain.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.520
There's no need to convert it into visual information.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.810
It's just an old habit.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:21.720
I still don't understand. You can directly access any data.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:28.970
I turned out to be incompatible, but in return, I can access your real raw data.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.470
How are the rookies?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.480
Epsilon's simulating the investigation.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.940
Of the serial murder case?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:38.980
Yeah.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.930
He wasn't satisfied with the investigation team's report,

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.950
although that's just a fragment of discontent in his psychological control system.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.650
Show me the most recent crime scene.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.810
Roger.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.920
The victim was stabbed once with a knife, causing his death.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.550
After the victim died, the culprit straddled his back and stabbed him ten or so more times.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.930
It's a typical random murder.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.390
Figured anything out, Mr. Novice Detective?

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:22.320
One advantage of being a cyborg is that I don't gain weight from eating popsicles.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.260
The cause of death was a bullet that fractured his cervical vertebrae.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.960
No sign of drugs or any particular disease.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.890
Small amounts of calcium carbonate and gypsum were found under his nails,

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.920
along with red and green dye.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.800
Dye, as in?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.360
Basically, chalk.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.800
Connect.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.610
What's the most frequent use of chalk these days?

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:55.000
Construction workers use them as markers.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:01.190
Pick up possible chalk users from nearby security cameras.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.850
Stop.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.110
Say...

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.190
Did the murderer draw this?

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.310
Connect.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.850
Show me prior visuals of this scene.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.210
Nothing out of the ordinary for the last five hours,

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:37.020
and recordings before that have already been deleted.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.650
Let's go back to the first crime scene.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.840
Even if you check it out, there might not be anything relevant.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.600
There's only one common thread.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:55.090
A person leading a normal life commits a murder because of psychological damage.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:06:00.120
And the post-murder investigation shows no psychological abnormalities.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.630
That other murderer died, though.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.940
Driving people insane enough to commit murder...

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:08.080
It sounds like a power they'd have.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.200
Connect.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.150
No larva signal was picked up at all, right?

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:16.810
No larva signal was detected at any of the scenes.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:21.930
It's not possible to drive someone insane without a larva burst.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.650
But there was no larva signal.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.960
Maybe it's a new ability.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.640
That's why I'm investigating.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.110
Connect.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.440
Replay the first scene, immediately after the crime.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.380
Should we go back?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:55.350
Yes, the doctor said I shouldn't put too much strength into rehab.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:57.380
Kiri.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.070
Yes?

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:03.160
You're going to that Fantasy something every day.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.140
No, I'm not saying it's bad.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.070
You've made friends, right?

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.240
I smell something sweet.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.070
Kiri?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.920
You don't need to suffer anymore.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.210
How could you do such a thing?

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:48.970
Goodness gracious. Kids these days!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.370
Okay?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.790
Target your voice here.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.550
Start whenever you're ready.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.020
Concentrate.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.730
One more time.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:43.360
Quon won't come to rescue you.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.620
I know it's tough, but it's for your own good.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.460
That's right.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:56.200
If you don't master your power,
you'll end up with ugly rashes like Yuri.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.380
Taka-bou!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.390
You're not exactly convincing,
considering that your own arm was injured!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.060
Yeah, is that so?

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.640
Your song heals people.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.820
But if you lose control, it becomes harmful.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:18.580
Oh, training. Nice to see someone so dedicated.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.570
Where's Quon?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.510
Investigating again.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:24.100
What a busy man.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.030
What are you saying?

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.570
You're just too much of a lazy bum!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.370
Oh come on, don't say that.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.890
Anyway, can I borrow her for a bit?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.220
I'd like you to babysit the kids here.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.290
But...

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.410
Stay focused!

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.120
Well, just let them do whatever they want.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.940
Everyone's having fun.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:02.160
No.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.410
It just looks that way.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.460
Hara's parents called her a monster.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:13.950
Takeru's house is under the complete control of the Custos.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:18.440
All the children here have special abilities.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.130
Here I go!

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.060
Hey, I bet you don't know this!

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:37.200
Only primates, which evolved their forelegs into arms, have the ability to throw.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.030
And even among the primates,

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:43.360
we humans are the only ones who can raise our arms and throw something.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.330
This is because we can—

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:47.930
Run away!

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:49.150
Now you've done it!

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.790
I'll get you brats!

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:51.780
Try and catch us!

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.690
Stop running!

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.160
In your dreams!

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.720
Why, you...

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:00.010
You're not getting away today!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.070
What are you doing?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:07.250
Since we're here, I'll take you to the base.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.020
Okay.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.190
Hello, and welcome.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.070
Is something wrong?

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.120
You're not hungry?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.040
I'm just happy we can be together.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.000
So am I.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.420
And Tei saw this?

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.330
Not exactly.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.900
She picked up a very dark feeling.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:37.990
We'll follow you.

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:48.540
Is this the best she has?

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.720
I don't understand you!

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.510
Stop barking!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:12:59.840
Another flower.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.840
I wonder if these old-fashioned graffiti are a recent fad.

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:10.630
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:14.940
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.900
What do you want?

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.280
Poor... flowers.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.480
Like you'd know anything!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.320
The flowers asked me to do this!

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.620
Geez!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.450
You're eating that again?

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.900
For a thousand years.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.180
Cup noodles are <i>the invention of the millennium,</i>

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:45.390
if you ask me.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.800
Yeah.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.820
How many so far this year?

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:53.920
Ten.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:56.810
There were 23 people I couldn't save.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.720
23 cases!

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.720
That's all we've accomplished!

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.970
Why do you think the Custos exist?

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:05.920
We're also doing our best.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:09.620
We didn't summon you to hear your excuses.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.420
You're here to be rebuked.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:15.410
The cyborg unit has been doing well lately.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.820
We're handling Insania—

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.830
Order can only be built on top of sacrifices.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:23.840
Who has been making the sacrifices to keep order?

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.450
We, the Ordo.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.750
How are Delta and Epsilon doing?

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.560
Shun and Hizuru?

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.040
Delta's and Epsilon's systems are both stable.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:49.360
Even after I removed their body parts,
their personalities haven't been affected.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.000
I don't see them anywhere.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.010
They're investigating the murder cases, apparently.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:57.890
They're analyzing the similarities one by one.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:01.440
They have very unique ways of going about it.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:02.980
It's very interesting.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.720
So their motive is curiosity.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.600
Their value is in capturing Bestia.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.230
Any other activity is superfluous.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.730
If they continue this too long, erase their data.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:18.480
That's not very fun.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:22.750
That would make them no different from AIs.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:27.990
Order can only be built on top of sacrifices.

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:31.490
Brutal...

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.450
And this weird scribble.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.360
It's a new pattern.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:39.440
Maybe the culprit's state of mind is changing.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:41.460
Perhaps he feels cornered.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.810
Download.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.050
And?

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:47.590
I looked up what flowers represent.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:51.700
In psychoanalysis, flowers carry a sexual meaning.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:53.260
Particularly for women.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.720
In Asia, they represent fragility.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.800
In Europe, they represent life.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:01.710
They also represent beauty and purity.

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:04.450
Flowers don't go well with murder.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:07.690
Still, most drugs come from plants.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.320
Marijuana is a widely known example,

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.630
and heroin is extracted from opium poppies.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:18.910
LSD is extracted from ergotamine on rye.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:24.610
Fungi like magic mushrooms and peyote carry hallucinogens.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.640
Though fungi aren't plants.

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:31.140
So flowers can also kill.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.320
Do you smell something?

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:48.930
I can as well.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.360
It's a sweet fragrance.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:55.610
I sensed it a bit at the last scene, and the one before.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:59.620
There's a smell associated with the murder?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.960
This could be the so-called Proust Effect.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.350
Proust?

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.350
He's a dead author.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:11.920
Marcel Proust is famous for the novel <i>In Search of Lost Time.</i>

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.260
At the beginning,

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:18.390
the protagonist remembers something because of the smell of madeleine dipped in tea.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:24.890
Now that you mention it, the old ladies in the kitchen were dipping rice crackers in tea.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:30.620
It's long been known that smells can help recover lost memories.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:35.400
The effect was named after the author, so, the Proust Effect.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.350
I see. I didn't know smells could do that.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.340
They can't.

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:41.610
But you just said...

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:47.400
The relationship between the sense of smell and memory is no different than with the other senses.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:52.460
However, odors activate the amygdalae, which control some memories.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.630
That's the limbic system.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:58.500
I'm talking about a part of the brain that heavily affects emotion.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:04.230
Basically, memories triggered by smell tend to pertain to emotions.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:09.950
What we want to know is if a smell could be used as a tool to kill.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.520
I was getting there.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:17.760
The amygdalae control emotions, and those include fear and rage, of course.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:23.570
If you could control someone's amygdalae,

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:26.380
you might be able to control the person.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.350
I wonder if it's really that simple.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.960
Larva signal, level red detected.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.580
One of our previous targets?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.720
No, it's new.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:44.070
Then from now on, we'll identify this larva as BF521.

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.690
Send in the WTOC.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:46.820
Roger.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:49.130
Alpha to Epsilon, move out.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.810
Condition all green.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:01.250
Perimeter has been blocked.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.450
Operation teams at their positions.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.490
Operation teams, follow the resistance protocol.

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:10.330
Roger.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:14.440
Operation teams, wait for the arrival of WTOC, then assist them.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:15.270
Roger.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:16.780
We'll wait for their arrival and—

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:18.510
What's wrong?

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:20.800
Operation teams, report your situation.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.400
What the hell is this?

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:38.930
Calm down.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:39.940
Avoid friendly fire.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:42.570
B-Seeker has arrived on the scene.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.330
Okay, kick off!

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:46.580
WTOC, kick off!

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:49.110
Formation 2-3!

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.260
That's as far as you go.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.020
Target BF521, larva burst confirmed.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.850
Switching to phase one.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.150
You monster...

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.620
What a pest.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.910
Epsilon's adrenaline level is rising.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:32.650
A psychokinesis type, huh.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.850
That's not very high on the priority list.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.340
If capturing it proves difficult, exterminate it.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:40.780
To all units, permission given to exterminate the target.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.970
This smell...

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.560
Flowers?

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:08.710
Target BF521 is dead.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.450
Recall them.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.200
Insania detected.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:34.880
Wait.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:38.410
We don't have time to prepare for a battle with Insania.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.240
We'll settle the score someday.

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:57.530
Another one... that I couldn't save.

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:03.190
Did you smell this fragrance?

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:16.960
Target BF521 drew this, huh?

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:21.320
Connect. Show me the footage of the time this was drawn.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:29.910
Pursue target BF521 from this point for as long as you can.

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:30.660
Roger.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:31.760
Wait.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:35.380
How many minutes before her death was the larva signal detected?

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:37.030
30 minutes.

00:22:37.030 --> 00:22:39.170
Show me the footage at that moment.

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.150
Roger.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:42.610
Stop.

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:44.050
Identify the flower.

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:50.040
It is the flower Sedirea Japonica.

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:52.550
It has a very unique fragrance.

00:22:53.650 --> 00:22:55.240
Is this a drawing of that flower?

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:58.080
It matches 62%.

00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:01.720
Tell the investigation unit to collect that flower.

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:02.330
Roger.

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:06.290
BF521 was responsible for all the cases.

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:10.190
Or... did the flower kill people?

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:22.160
Let's stop here for today.

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:23.870
You're working hard.

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:25.460
Old man.

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.080
Here.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.780
That's for working hard.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:32.720
Candy.

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:55.590
Why... did you stomp on the flowers?

00:23:59.610 --> 00:24:00.450
What are you doing?

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:04.880
Follow me.

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:09.880
Hey, wait up!

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.100
Hello!

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:23.240
Here you go.

00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:28.150
It's a gift.

00:24:28.150 --> 00:24:29.360
Have fun.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:37.490
Wow!

00:24:38.790 --> 00:24:40.470
They're all so happy!

00:24:41.110 --> 00:24:43.880
I've never seen a garden this vigorous!

00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:45.390
Um...

00:24:46.510 --> 00:24:47.580
What's your name?

00:24:49.880 --> 00:24:51.260
Kaoru.

00:24:53.920 --> 00:24:56.030
I'm Kiri.

00:24:59.850 --> 00:25:01.220
Do you like it?

00:25:01.810 --> 00:25:03.080
Tei-san!

00:25:03.060 --> 00:25:05.190
Did you make this garden?

00:25:05.190 --> 00:25:07.220
It wasn't me.

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:09.040
Quon-sama made it.

00:25:09.040 --> 00:25:10.170
Quon?

00:25:10.170 --> 00:25:12.280
Is he here?

00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:15.140
No, he's not here at the moment.

00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:19.120
I bet he understands flowers very well.

00:25:19.940 --> 00:25:22.660
None of the flowers here are suffering.

00:25:22.660 --> 00:25:24.630
They're all loved.

00:25:24.630 --> 00:25:27.980
They're not being forced to bloom.

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:31.130
That's why they're all beautiful.

00:25:31.130 --> 00:25:35.010
A normal garden is screaming in pain.

00:25:35.010 --> 00:25:39.630
No one gives them love, but they're forced to bloom.

00:25:39.630 --> 00:25:42.580
They're all crying.

00:25:42.580 --> 00:25:45.300
That's why... That's why I...

00:25:46.560 --> 00:25:48.400
The flowers asked me to do this!

00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:52.390
The flowers asked you?

00:25:52.390 --> 00:25:58.600
They said they were suffering,
and they'd rather be stomped to death.

00:25:58.600 --> 00:26:01.440
You can hear the voice of the flowers?

00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:03.400
What a weirdo.

00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:04.970
That's strange.

00:26:04.970 --> 00:26:06.610
Hey, don't say that!

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:08.700
Flowers can't talk!

00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:11.040
Hey, you can't say that!

00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:13.000
But that's not normal!

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:15.060
He's a weirdo!

00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:16.260
What a weirdo.

00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:18.240
Stay away!

00:26:18.220 --> 00:26:19.470
Yeah!

00:26:19.470 --> 00:26:22.030
Why am I so different?

00:26:22.030 --> 00:26:22.890
You're weird.

00:26:22.890 --> 00:26:23.930
No!

00:26:23.930 --> 00:26:27.660
You're the weirdos because you can't hear their voices!

00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:30.180
Wait!

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:36.950
What a pain.

00:26:36.950 --> 00:26:40.070
Does that dog really know what she's following?

00:26:41.750 --> 00:26:43.770
The scent is our only lead.

00:26:43.770 --> 00:26:46.060
That's not very helpful.

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:49.210
For the time being, it's the only thing we can follow.

00:26:49.210 --> 00:26:52.000
Maybe he's closer to us than we think.

00:27:01.730 --> 00:27:07.310
Anyone who laughs at me should just go ahead and die!

00:27:09.300 --> 00:27:12.340
Hey, what are you going to do when you find him?

00:27:12.340 --> 00:27:15.170
He's killed many people.

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:17.190
Are you going to save that criminal?

00:27:17.190 --> 00:27:20.930
Are you saying it's okay for the Custos to kill him because he's sinned?

00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:27.200
Then I should be the first one to die.

00:27:27.200 --> 00:27:28.510
Quon...

00:27:28.510 --> 00:27:32.120
I bear a sin much greater than his.

00:27:39.990 --> 00:27:41.490
Did you find him?

00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:44.090
Maybe he's already gone home.

00:27:44.090 --> 00:27:49.870
I told those kids not to laugh at other people's abilities.

00:27:54.270 --> 00:27:56.470
Everyone should just die!

00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:57.820
Go crazy!

00:27:57.820 --> 00:27:59.790
What was his problem?

00:28:00.310 --> 00:28:02.510
You finally found him?

00:28:19.980 --> 00:28:22.980
Hey guys, I'm home.

00:28:23.850 --> 00:28:25.100
Here?

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:27.580
Okay.

00:28:41.170 --> 00:28:42.560
He's here.

00:28:43.610 --> 00:28:44.610
I know you're in there!

00:28:44.610 --> 00:28:46.410
Come out!

00:28:50.690 --> 00:28:52.130
I knew it.

00:28:57.920 --> 00:28:59.800
What are you gonna do? Are you coming in?

00:29:00.690 --> 00:29:02.050
Of course!

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:08.760
Look, you...

00:29:10.060 --> 00:29:11.010
Aren't you scared?

00:29:19.170 --> 00:29:23.590
I can make flowers release smells that make people afraid,

00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:27.350
that drive them insane.

00:29:27.350 --> 00:29:29.700
Is that how you made them crazy?

00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:32.960
Everyone was crazy from the start.

00:29:32.960 --> 00:29:37.180
The flowers are screaming in pain, and no one's trying to help them.

00:29:37.170 --> 00:29:37.880
Still, you can't...

00:29:37.880 --> 00:29:40.250
They all say I'm weird!

00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:44.010
Come to the Fantasium Garden.

00:29:44.010 --> 00:29:46.260
Then you'll...

00:29:46.260 --> 00:29:48.750
I was just there.

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:50.720
I hate that place!

00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:52.420
What?

00:29:52.420 --> 00:29:56.120
Everyone there was smiling. It was gross.

00:29:56.120 --> 00:29:58.030
It looked fake.

00:29:58.030 --> 00:30:01.680
Oh, the garden was kind of nice.

00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:03.730
Kind of.

00:30:03.730 --> 00:30:06.390
But the people there are terrible.

00:30:06.400 --> 00:30:11.030
They say they have abilities, but they laughed at mine and said it's weird.

00:30:11.770 --> 00:30:13.790
They should all go to Hell.

00:30:13.790 --> 00:30:14.920
You didn't!

00:30:16.480 --> 00:30:17.640
I did.

00:30:17.640 --> 00:30:19.370
No... Tei...

00:30:19.370 --> 00:30:20.940
Tei, can you hear me?

00:30:20.920 --> 00:30:22.750
Tei?

00:30:23.450 --> 00:30:26.230
Okay, I'll tell Quon-sama.

00:30:27.470 --> 00:30:32.560
The flower that's causing the murders is somewhere in the Fantasium Garden?

00:30:32.560 --> 00:30:34.580
Stupid Taka-bou...

00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:36.870
The culprit caught him.

00:30:36.870 --> 00:30:38.750
Yuri, go to the garden.

00:30:38.730 --> 00:30:39.560
What will you do?

00:30:39.560 --> 00:30:41.560
I'll save him.

00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:42.940
That's you all right.

00:30:42.940 --> 00:30:44.970
Take care of Taka-bou, okay?

00:30:44.970 --> 00:30:47.370
I also need to save the culprit.

00:30:49.100 --> 00:30:50.370
Quon...

00:30:51.330 --> 00:30:54.040
I guess there's no choice.

00:30:56.470 --> 00:31:00.960
Thank you for coming to the Fantasium Garden today.

00:30:59.290 --> 00:31:00.960
I'm sorry.

00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:04.450
We unexpectedly have to do some maintenance.

00:31:04.450 --> 00:31:07.030
Yay! I got a balloon!

00:31:07.840 --> 00:31:08.760
How's it going?

00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:10.210
I don't know.

00:31:10.220 --> 00:31:14.100
Too many locations in the Garden have plants.

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:17.440
Find it at all cost, before there's another victim.

00:31:15.330 --> 00:31:16.950
Did you find it?

00:31:16.930 --> 00:31:18.480
No.

00:31:17.440 --> 00:31:18.480
Of course!

00:31:23.310 --> 00:31:24.780
This smell...

00:31:27.860 --> 00:31:29.860
No... Quon-san...

00:31:35.530 --> 00:31:37.540
No!

00:31:39.910 --> 00:31:42.280
Shoot! She's panicked!

00:31:42.280 --> 00:31:44.420
She's going to destroy our shield.

00:31:44.420 --> 00:31:46.270
If that happens...

00:31:46.250 --> 00:31:49.010
...the Custos will find this place!

00:31:51.160 --> 00:31:52.920
What can we do?

00:31:52.920 --> 00:31:55.320
Someone needs to jump in there!

00:31:58.180 --> 00:32:00.440
Hey, don't push me!

00:32:01.510 --> 00:32:02.980
You useless men!

00:32:07.120 --> 00:32:07.980
Get a grip!

00:32:17.030 --> 00:32:18.770
Ow...

00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:19.810
Yuri!

00:32:19.790 --> 00:32:20.790
Are you okay?

00:32:20.790 --> 00:32:23.050
I think I broke a few ribs this time.

00:32:23.040 --> 00:32:24.170
How's Kiri-chan?

00:32:26.670 --> 00:32:28.720
I think she's fine.

00:32:29.670 --> 00:32:31.290
Yuri-san!

00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:33.580
You're okay now.

00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:46.560
Don't run away.

00:32:46.560 --> 00:32:50.430
If you run away, this will happen again somewhere else.

00:32:50.430 --> 00:32:54.570
We want to prevent that, so stay and learn how to control your power.

00:32:54.570 --> 00:32:56.040
Okay?

00:32:58.700 --> 00:33:00.030
Okay!

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:03.680
Good girl.

00:33:06.080 --> 00:33:08.190
It seems that...

00:33:09.430 --> 00:33:11.570
the flower at the Fantasium Garden failed.

00:33:11.570 --> 00:33:13.830
And they've found this place too.

00:33:14.630 --> 00:33:16.510
I'm going to get yelled at anyway...

00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:19.060
so I might as well do it.

00:33:19.850 --> 00:33:24.060
Phalaenopsis. Vuylstekeara. Paphiopedilum.

00:33:25.390 --> 00:33:29.390
The collected Sedirea Japonica were perfectly normal?

00:33:29.390 --> 00:33:31.550
Yes, nothing abnormal.

00:33:31.550 --> 00:33:34.560
Does the effect disappear after a certain time?

00:33:35.800 --> 00:33:37.510
Larva signal detected.

00:33:37.510 --> 00:33:39.740
The target is BF502.

00:33:39.740 --> 00:33:42.110
Alpha to Epsilon, move out.

00:33:48.500 --> 00:33:49.400
Miu!

00:33:52.370 --> 00:33:53.500
It's dangerous.

00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:54.690
Get out of here now.

00:33:55.410 --> 00:33:58.240
No, please do as I say.

00:34:13.800 --> 00:34:16.110
Who are you?

00:34:17.620 --> 00:34:19.120
I'm sorry.

00:34:19.110 --> 00:34:22.620
I wanted to save you before this happened.

00:34:22.620 --> 00:34:24.040
Save me?

00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:26.030
What are you talking about?

00:34:26.030 --> 00:34:29.820
I'm wondering why I never tried this from the start!

00:34:29.820 --> 00:34:30.950
Stop!

00:34:30.950 --> 00:34:33.580
Only the weak do this!

00:34:41.070 --> 00:34:43.670
I'm stronger than anyone.

00:34:43.670 --> 00:34:46.480
I can even rule the world.

00:34:48.770 --> 00:34:49.770
I can't...

00:34:50.900 --> 00:34:53.240
die.

00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:54.720
I see.

00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:57.580
Then how many times should I kill you?

00:35:09.150 --> 00:35:10.330
Stop!

00:35:11.810 --> 00:35:13.280
Stop...

00:35:14.410 --> 00:35:17.330
You're wrong.

00:35:19.500 --> 00:35:21.350
You're boring.

00:35:21.340 --> 00:35:23.800
You say the same thing over and over,

00:35:23.800 --> 00:35:26.180
and you don't even die?

00:35:26.180 --> 00:35:27.770
That's unfair.

00:35:30.810 --> 00:35:31.730
Takao!

00:35:31.730 --> 00:35:33.610
Ah, so you know him!

00:35:33.610 --> 00:35:36.500
Will he... die?

00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:44.950
That's right!

00:35:44.950 --> 00:35:47.720
You can't do a thing!

00:36:17.820 --> 00:36:19.390
Insania detected.

00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:20.070
Where?

00:36:20.070 --> 00:36:23.200
Near BF502.

00:36:23.960 --> 00:36:27.080
Insania and BF502 confirmed.

00:36:27.080 --> 00:36:28.960
Formation 4-7.

00:36:50.620 --> 00:36:54.120
Gamma's amygdalae are showing abnormal levels.

00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:56.490
We're disconnecting him now.

00:36:56.490 --> 00:36:58.830
Gamma, disconnected nervous system.

00:37:03.490 --> 00:37:07.320
Without Gamma, it'll be difficult to retrieve the target.

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:12.070
It's an interesting ability, but I suppose we'll wait for another time.

00:37:12.070 --> 00:37:13.750
Exterminate it.

00:37:13.750 --> 00:37:14.700
Roger.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:16.530
Formation 0-3!

00:37:18.290 --> 00:37:19.390
Stop this now!

00:37:22.420 --> 00:37:24.880
No!

00:37:25.890 --> 00:37:26.990
Now!

00:37:58.220 --> 00:37:59.990
You fucking monster!

00:38:31.280 --> 00:38:34.790
Larva burst, level 5.

00:38:40.590 --> 00:38:43.330
You should all turn into flowers.

00:38:46.280 --> 00:38:50.770
How about I tear you apart the way you humans kill flowers?!

00:38:54.990 --> 00:38:57.850
You can hear the voices of the flowers?

00:38:58.600 --> 00:39:00.910
What about the voices of humans?

00:39:00.910 --> 00:39:02.530
I can hear them!

00:39:02.530 --> 00:39:04.790
They all say I'm weird!

00:39:04.790 --> 00:39:06.550
That's right.

00:39:06.550 --> 00:39:09.300
No one tried to listen to you.

00:39:10.200 --> 00:39:12.630
What you did is wrong.

00:39:12.630 --> 00:39:17.140
But... you just wanted someone to listen to you, right?

00:39:21.850 --> 00:39:23.290
Particle gun, fire!

00:39:23.870 --> 00:39:24.790
Get away!

00:39:42.270 --> 00:39:47.270
If you meet the gardener at the Fantasium Garden,

00:39:47.270 --> 00:39:50.160
then tell him that it's a very beautiful garden.

00:39:50.160 --> 00:39:52.300
Tell him yourself!

00:39:52.300 --> 00:39:53.800
It's fine.

00:39:53.800 --> 00:39:56.810
No one will care if I die.

00:39:56.810 --> 00:39:59.440
Don't you dare say that!

00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:17.890
Is he crying?

00:40:17.890 --> 00:40:21.330
Those monsters don't have those human emotions.

00:40:22.520 --> 00:40:24.020
Retreat.

00:40:24.020 --> 00:40:26.450
We're low on operational margin.

00:40:26.450 --> 00:40:28.530
We had a tough time against Insania,

00:40:28.530 --> 00:40:31.990
but we gave him a tough time too.

00:40:39.640 --> 00:40:41.280
How is she?

00:40:41.280 --> 00:40:43.940
I specialize in humans.

00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:46.890
Still, I've done my best.

00:40:46.890 --> 00:40:47.590
Azuki!

00:40:48.090 --> 00:40:50.130
Azuki!

00:40:50.130 --> 00:40:51.900
I'm sorry.

00:40:51.900 --> 00:40:53.630
Azuki won't die!

00:40:53.630 --> 00:40:55.740
She can't die!

00:40:55.740 --> 00:40:56.470
What the hell?

00:40:56.470 --> 00:40:58.230
I'm hurt too,

00:40:58.230 --> 00:41:01.150
but you're all worried about the dog?

00:41:01.150 --> 00:41:03.840
She was injured trying to save you!

00:41:03.850 --> 00:41:05.480
I know!

00:41:05.480 --> 00:41:08.150
We don't have time for your jokes!

00:41:08.150 --> 00:41:09.020
Kiri!

00:41:09.020 --> 00:41:11.320
You could save her, right?

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:15.580
Kiri, please...

00:41:16.070 --> 00:41:17.310
But...

00:41:18.850 --> 00:41:21.830
Do you think you'll go berserk again?

00:41:25.320 --> 00:41:28.790
You've been training very hard.

00:41:31.920 --> 00:41:35.910
Do you think you didn't choose your power?

00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:38.540
Well, you're wrong.

00:41:39.490 --> 00:41:42.790
The power you wish for from the bottom of your heart...

00:41:42.790 --> 00:41:44.930
is the ability you awaken to.

00:42:20.990 --> 00:42:22.410
Quon!

00:42:22.390 --> 00:42:24.720
I was able to sing well.

00:42:25.380 --> 00:42:26.370
I see.

00:42:26.370 --> 00:42:27.990
Good for you.

00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:32.230
That flower...

00:42:32.230 --> 00:42:33.710
It's safe.

00:42:33.690 --> 00:42:35.740
It's not emitting a dangerous fragrance anymore.

00:42:40.620 --> 00:42:44.610
No one will make fun of you here.

00:42:44.620 --> 00:42:47.620
I'm sorry I never got your name.

00:42:48.720 --> 00:42:50.110
Kaoru.

00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:55.050
His name.

00:42:56.730 --> 00:42:58.060
Thank you.

00:42:59.560 --> 00:43:03.350
Kaoru-kun, good night.

00:43:12.560 --> 00:43:17.610
Feel Rock emotion! Burning Rock emotion!

00:43:17.610 --> 00:43:25.830
A scream of my burning soul that seems to burst out of my chest

00:43:17.610 --> 00:43:25.620
mune no oku hajike sou na atsui tamashii no sakebi wo

00:43:25.830 --> 00:43:32.380
Burst on the fire

00:43:46.100 --> 00:43:51.230
I was struck by thunderstorm, suddenly awakening my instinct

00:43:46.100 --> 00:43:51.230
raiu ni utare totsuzen mezameta honnou

00:43:51.230 --> 00:43:55.770
It burns on, pushing aside my sensibility

00:43:51.230 --> 00:43:55.770
risei wo oshinokete moetagiru no sa

00:43:55.770 --> 00:44:00.860
The truth is written on the walls of memory

00:43:55.770 --> 00:44:00.860
kioku no kabe ni kakikomareta shinjitsu wa

00:44:00.860 --> 00:44:05.200
No one can violate it

00:44:00.860 --> 00:44:05.080
dare ni mo okasenai

00:44:05.200 --> 00:44:14.630
We have no questions; we just want to break the structure of this world with our hands

00:44:05.330 --> 00:44:14.580
